  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively connect temperature-dependent mechanical response in HEAs with dislocation density, lattice distortion, stacking faults/FCC-HCP behavior, elastic-modulus degradation, and high-temperature softening. R5 additionally establishes elevated-temperature friction and wear testing of an HEA coating, while R6 and R17 suggest retention of strength at intermediate temperature followed by thermally activated softening. However, none describes temperature-controlled nanoindentation/friction simulation of an FeNiCrCoCu coating on Cu, nor the specific transition near 900 K from stacking-fault-mediated deformation to lattice disorder accompanied by dislocation-density loss and increased friction. Thus the literature points in the right direction, but combining these elements into the later intervention and mechanism requires a substantial new idea."
